# Enterprise Inline Editing Pattern

Adopt contextual inline editing across Nexora profile, detail, and master-record workspaces.

Canonical references:
- `docs/06-guidelines/NEXORA_PLATFORM_UX_CONSTITUTION.md` (sections 7–8)
- `docs/06-guidelines/INLINE_EDITING_STANDARD.md`

## Core Principle

Everything looks editable. Not everything is directly editable.

- Fields owned by the current entity: inline save via `EditableField`.
- Fields owned by another engine: open the correct workflow via `onWorkflowOpen` — never direct DB updates.

## Required Platform Components

Use shared components from `@/shared/ui`:

- `EditableField` — single-field inline editing
- `EditableSectionCard` — sectioned profile/detail cards
- `useEditableField` — save/validation state
- `EntityLookup` — all relations (never expose raw IDs)
- `DatePicker` / `DatePickerField` — all dates (never `<input type="date">`)
- `platform.feedback` — success/error toasts (never Sonner directly)

## Profile And Detail Pages

- Every profile is a workspace with independently editable sections.
- Use `EditableSectionCard` with header actions: Edit, History, Audit, Collapse.
- Replace monolithic edit pages with tabbed/sectioned inline editing.
- List pages still use `RecordFormDialog` modal pattern for create/edit.

## Permissions

- Lack of permission → visible read-only field with lock icon and tooltip.
- Hide fields only when security policy requires it.
- Enforce permissions server-side and via RLS — not UI-only.

## Saving

- Validate client + server + business rules.
- Record audit: who, when, old value, new value, reason.
- Optimistic update where safe.
- Refresh only the affected section — never full page reload.

## Auto Save

Allowed only for notes, descriptions, and comments. Never for financial, assignment, contract, payroll, or inventory values.

## Prohibited

- Standalone full-page edit routes for simple master/profile data
- Module-local inline edit primitives
- Raw UUID fields for relations
- Native date inputs
- Direct cross-engine field mutation from inline editors

## New Screens

Every new screen across Platform, HR, Finance, SCM, Manufacturing, CRM, Commerce, Fleet, Projects, Service, and POS must follow this pattern unless a wizard or document lifecycle explicitly requires otherwise.
